{{!--
  Signing in to a connected application with the wallet.

  Nothing on this page asks the holder to identify themselves. The browser shows
  a challenge; the wallet answers it with its own Wallet ID. The page then posts
  the challenge — not a subject — back to the authorization endpoint.

  Wallet is the only method offered. Passkey, Verified ID and YubiKey are real
  sign-in methods elsewhere in the platform, but they are not wired into this
  endpoint yet and a button that cannot finish is worse than no button at all.
--}}
<section class="page-hero page-hero--compact">
  <p class="eyebrow">Aegis ID</p>
  <h1>Approve this sign-in from your wallet.</h1>
  <p>
    <strong>{{appName}}</strong> wants to know it is really you. Scan the code
    below, or open the link on the phone your wallet is installed on.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="band band--white">
  <div class="auth-grid auth-grid--compact">
    <div class="auth-panel">
      <div class="auth-panel__form" data-wallet-signin="{{challengeId}}">
        <h2>Scan with the Aegis ID wallet</h2>

        <div class="wallet-signin__qr">
          <img src="{{qrCodeDataUrl}}" alt="QR code containing this sign-in request" width="240" height="240">
        </div>

        <p class="form-footnote wallet-signin__link">{{deepLink}}</p>

        <p>
          <a class="button button--primary" href="{{deepLink}}">Open in my wallet</a>
        </p>

        <p class="form-footnote" data-wallet-signin-status role="status" aria-live="polite">
          Waiting for your wallet. This request expires in about {{expiresInMinutes}} minutes.
        </p>

        {{!--
          The values the completion call needs. Held as data rather than as a
          form, because the authorization endpoint answers with a redirect to
          the relying party's origin and `form-action 'self'` would block that
          whole chain. The page navigates itself instead.
        --}}
        <span hidden
          data-wallet-signin-client="{{clientId}}"
          data-wallet-signin-redirect="{{redirectUri}}"
          data-wallet-signin-response="{{responseType}}"
          data-wallet-signin-org="{{organizationId}}"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why there is nothing to fill in</p>
      <h2>Your device answers, not a form.</h2>
      <p>
        Your wallet presents its own Wallet ID from its own storage. Nothing in
        the code above names you, which is what makes it safe to show on a
        screen anyone can photograph — somebody else scanning it signs in as
        themselves, not as you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once approved, you will be able to choose which of your organizations to
        act in. One wallet holds credentials from as many organizations as have
        issued to you.
      </p>
      <p class="form-footnote">
        No wallet yet? <a href="/support">Support</a> explains how to set one up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
